Stages (aka targets):

base - setup debian system, installs rcheckserver + build-dep; build args:
  DEBIAN_TAG=unstable - which debian base image to use (testing, unstable, stable etc.)
  DEBIAN_MIRROR=http://deb.debian.org - mirror to use 
 
build-r (uses base) - sets up build scripts and R-devel sources; the entrypoint builds R in /build (see entry-build-r.sh); args:
  R_BUILD_SYSDEPS - any additional system package to install in the image at build time (e.g. BLAS)
  UID=1000, GID=1000 - uid/gid of the rbuild user (can match the local one, but doesn't have to)

the entrypoint passes any arguments to build-R and also honors the following env vars:
MAKE, MAKEFLAGS and NO_UPDATE (see below)

pkgcheck (uses build-r) - this one is just trivial image to run entry-pkgcheck.sh which
  is just a call to check_packages_in_dir()
  it works off /pkg (if mounted) or /build/pkg (if re-using the /build mount).
  It will require R built with the above build-r image.

Example usage:

## create image from debian:unstable with NZ mirror to build R with OpenBLAS and tag is as rchk-build-r:unstable-openblas
docker build \
  --build-arg DEBIAN_TAG=unstable \
  --build-arg DEBIAN_MIRROR=http://ftp.nz.debian.org \
  --build-arg UID=$(id -u) --build-arg GID=$(id -g) \
  --build-arg R_BUILD_SYSDEPS=libopenblas-dev \
  --target build-r -t rchk-build-r:unstable-openblas .

## run the image to build R with OpenBLAS in the "build" directory, use 64 cores
## and don’t update /src (QA+R) from SVN, remove the container when done:
mkdir build
docker run -it --rm -v $(pwd)/build:/build \
  -e MAKEFLAGS=-j64 \
  -e NO_UPDATE=1 \
  rchk-build-r:unstable-openblas -bo

## build pkgcheck image based on the above (will be almost a no-op)
docker build \
  --build-arg DEBIAN_TAG=unstable \
  --build-arg DEBIAN_MIRROR=http://ftp.nz.debian.org \
  --build-arg UID=$(id -u) --build-arg GID=$(id -g) \
  --build-arg R_BUILD_SYSDEPS=libopenblas-dev \
  --target pkgcheck -t rchk-pkgcheck:unstable-openblas .

put any packages in build/pkg, so example usage:

mkdir build/pkg
(cd build/pkg && curl -LO https://rforge.net/Cairo/snapshot/Cairo_1.7-1.tar.gz )
docker run --rm -v $(pwd)/build:/build rchk-pkgcheck:unstable-openblas



